ver should read at that point — and, for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen."}]},{"text":"Refreshing without losing data","anchor":"Refreshing-without-losing-data","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" always shows "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" first, which is right for the initial fetch but wrong for pull-to-refresh — the list shouldn’t disappear behind a spinner while it’s being refetched. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead: it keeps the current "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" on screen while the operation runs, and leaves it there if the operation fails instead of switching to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["List(articles) { article in","    Text(article.title)","}",".refreshable {","    await store.refreshCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the duration; a failure is reported via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than by discarding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":", so the list stays visible and you can surface the error separately (a toast, for example)."}]},{"text":"Retrying on failure","anchor":"Retrying-on-failure","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a flaky call worth retrying automatically before showing an error, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive